From: Nexus Battlesuit <james@nexus.ai>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 19:54:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Remove dangerous WARN_ON_ONCE in __pick_eevdf

__pick_eevdf() is called with the rq->lock held. Calling WARN_ON_ONCE()
triggered a circular locking dependency between the rq->lock and
console_lock in some scenarios, leading to a kernel deadlock.

Remove the warning as it is primarily for debugging and the system
stability is prioritized in this critical path.

Signed-off-by: Nexus Battlesuit <james@nexus.ai>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 387418..42815 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1027,8 +1027,6 @@ static struct sched_entity *__pick_eevdf(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, bool protect)
 	 */
 	if (sched_feat(PICK_BUDDY) &&
 	    cfs_rq->next && entity_eligible(cfs_rq, cfs_rq->next)) {
-		/* ->next will never be delayed */
-		WARN_ON_ONCE(cfs_rq->next->sched_delayed);
 		return cfs_rq->next;
 	}
 
-- 
